The '''Vaathkree Trade Corridor''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that ran between the celestial body [[Corsin]] on the [[Hydian Way]] and the astronomical object [[Gizer]] on the [[Perlemian Trade Route]]. It passed through the [[Expansion Region]], [[Inner Rim Territories]], [[Mid Rim Territories]], and [[New Territories]]. [[Galactic Republic]] [[scout ship]]s traveled up the route before discovering the [[Ubdurian]] [[Ubdurians' empire|trade empire]].

==Description==
The Vaathkree Trade Corridor was a [[hyperspace route]] that shared its name<ref name="AotG" /> with the [[Outer Rim Territories]] astronomical object [[Vaathkree system|Vaathkree]].<ref name="TFABG" /> One terminus of the route was the [[Expansion Region]] celestial body [[Corsin]] on the [[Hydian Way]].<ref name="TFABG" /> The trade route ran from Corsin to<ref name="GM" /> the [[Ubdurian]] [[homeworld]]<ref name="AA">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> [[Ubduria]] in the [[Inner Rim Territories]], which in turn linked to [[Obroa-skai]],<ref name="GM" /> a [[planet]] in the Inner Rim's [[Obroa-skai system]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> Both these locations also fell within the [[New Territories]] region of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="NewTerritories" />

From there, the route passed through the Expansion Region again and then over the border into the [[Mid Rim Territories]], where it passed through the celestial body [[Contruum]] and [[Montross]], a planet located in the [[Montross system]],<ref name="Dawn" /> before terminating at [[Gizer]], an astronomical object on the [[Perlemian Trade Route]].<ref name="GM" /> The planet [[Telerath]] in the [[Nouane sector]]'s [[Telerath system]] also fell somewhere along the Inner Rim portion of the route.<ref name="Knights of Fate" /> The Vaathkree Trade Corridor fell within squares M-7, N-7, N-8, O-8, and P-8 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="GM" />

==History==
[[Scout ship]]s from the [[Galactic Republic]] traveled along the Vaathkree Trade Corridor before discovering the territory of the Ubdurians' [[Ubdurians' empire|trade empire]].<ref name="AotG" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Carest_space.png|thumb|right|300px|The Vaathkree Trade Corridor originated in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity.]]
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Vaathkree Trade Corridor was first pictured in "The History of Neimoidia," an article in the "[[Guide to the Galaxy]]" department of the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 52|fifty-second]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF 52">{{BuildFalconCite|52|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> published around [[December 30]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|52}}</ref> The route was first identified in ''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]'', a [[2016]] reference book written by [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="AotG" />

The [[Vaathkree Trade Corridor/Legends|Vaathkree Trade Corridor]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned in "[[Heroes Need Not Apply]]," an article written by [[Tony Russo|Anthony P. Russo]] and [[Eric S. Trautmann]] and published by [[West End Games]] in the [[Star Wars Adventure Journal 12|twelfth issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars Adventure Journal]]'' series in [[February]], [[1997]].<ref name="SWAJ12">{{JournalCite|12|Heroes Need Not Apply}}</ref> It was then depicted for the first time in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', which was written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

